  "cover_text": "The court system in Sheridan, Arkansas is a government-run chicken farm running a sheep farm.\n\nThe court system awards mandatory checks each and every year to the private industrial hemp program run by the Arkansas Department of Agriculture.\n\nElizedo says the ten block farms outshone the predominately government-run farms, suggesting that the state legislature badly needed to reconsider its annual allotment of farmland.\n\nElizedo says government bureaucrats hired the Armstrong horses to do it for them.\n\n\"We hired it anyway, even though the company is for federal farm subsidy and county staff are ineligible,\" Elizedo says.\n\nAnother county worker took a chance on setting up a liaison from the",
